<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lord Charles Somerset</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1767–1831</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lord Charles <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a> was a British soldier and politician who governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> from 1814 to 1826. He ruled in an autocratic manner, made English the official language of government and encouraged the settlement of the 1820 Settlers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a>. His clashes with the free press and his handling of the eastern frontier with the Xhosa led to his recall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lord-charles-somerset.jpg" alt="Lord Charles Somerset" width="216" height="298" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lord_Charles_Henry_Somerset.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
